# auth roles are internal only (for now)

there is **no customer web portal** yet. auth + `profiles.role` + rls only support **staff**:

- `admin`
- `cashier`
- `kitchen`

## do not

- add end-customer / member / “user” logins on top of the same `user_role` enum without a redesign
- reuse staff rls (`orders` select for all authenticated kitchen/admin patterns, inventory reads, etc.) for public accounts

## why it will break if you bolt users on

- `current_user_role()` and policies assume every `authenticated` identity is staff
- kitchen/admin need broad `orders` / `order_items` select; a customer account under the same policies could inherit the wrong access or get blocked in confusing ways
- middleware sends unknown/missing roles toward staff homes / login — no customer destination
- public surface today is **anon** `/menu` only (read menu), not logged-in customers

## when customers are added later

- new role space (e.g. `customer`) **or** separate auth surface / table
- explicit rls: customers see **only their** orders (and never inventory/waste/admin)
- keep staff policies scoped to internal roles (`in ('admin','cashier','kitchen')`), never “any authenticated”
- treat as a deliberate phase + migrations — not a quick enum add

## current public access

- qr `/menu` = `anon` select on categories/products/modifiers only
- ordering stays at the truck (pos), not a customer checkout portal
